{"id": "EUVD-2026-20517", "enisaUuid": "ebc61a34-71b4-394d-a5b5-6fa5e3b4393b", "description": "A flaw was found in Red Hat Quay's Proxy Cache configuration feature. When an organization administrator configures an upstream registry for proxy caching, Quay makes a network connection to the specified registry hostname without verifying that it points to a legitimate external service. An attacker with organization administrator privileges could supply a crafted hostname to force the Quay server to make requests to internal network services, cloud infrastructure endpoints, or other resources that should not be accessible from the Quay application.", "datePublished": "2026-04-08T17:06:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-22T17:59:55", "baseScore": 5.2, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:N", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:24833", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:40262", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:41031", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:41066", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:42146", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:42796", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:43052", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:48085", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:70267", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-32591", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2446965"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-32591", "GHSA-9wjq-f6rc-86wf"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "324f33f0-e2cb-3f08-9173-955114374511", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Quay 3.10", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1783750447"}, {"id": "3edd5920-dffc-3617-a9c8-6aeb20da677d", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Quay 3.9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1784125838"}, {"id": "430fcfda-1fb7-328e-8638-f0e6c41de0bd", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Quay 3.17", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_v